      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be really case by case. In my experiment with real workload, I never have seen such short-term pinning so test_pages_isolated would be helpful. In the opposite case, I easily see test_pages_isolated constantly failed.\nActually, I don\u0027t think that kinds of hope(i.e. migrate_pages failed but the very next test_pages isolated will be succeeded since someone drop the page reference count during the window) does make sense.\nIf you concerned the way, we could hide it under only GFP_NORETRY.\nI have no problem. Just transition from existing cma alloc user to the GFP_NORETRY users.",
